{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/381134-boo-ma-no-hands-demon-house-and-manipulating-stuff","id":381134,"title":"Boo Ma, No Hands!- Demon House and Manipulating Stuff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-25T10:38:22-08:00","id":381134,"title":"Boo Ma, No Hands!- Demon House and Manipulating Stuff","content":"So, strictly speaking from the reading of Demon House, You can appear in mirrors(reflective surfaces, whatever), speak to people, and use embeds and exploits. Nothing about this implies that you can move stuff around or such. I think I've got this right, but if I'm wrong, now's the time to find out.<br /> <br /> I get the idea of this from a design perspective, because the power is already <i>really</i> powerful in that it allows you to get basic omniscience for the building you possess and allows you a window to attack people without really getting hit for cheap(Yay 2 EXP). Adding 'hands' both makes it too powerful and strays from the idea of demons being powerfully subtle creatures. I also understand that limitations are what make the game interesting. That said, I'm wondering if on top of misunderstanding or missing something from the rules, I'm also wondering if there're other elements to the power that make adding a light ability to move things a bad idea.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure I'm not going to change the power, because I like pushing players to think outside the box, but I did share in their disappointment last night when they found the edges of the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T19:37:21-08:00","id":381535,"title":"","content":"From a mechanical standpoint: they can use other embeds, exploits and form abilities. Trick of the Light, Recurring Hallucinations and others fill most of the gaps you describe.<br /> <br /> From a storytelling perspective: whatever makes a better story. If the limitations on Demon House frustrate you and your players, do away with them and don't look back. I those same limitations force your players to improvise and act creatively, keep them.<br /> <br /> To split the difference, Flowers of Hell discusses the concept of learning embeds and exploits as a gnostic experience: sudden bursts of insight into their old power. You could let your players just pay for (or even go into debt) embeds if the mood of the session feels appropriate for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T20:41:41-08:00","id":381558,"title":"","content":"Does it allow form abilities? That alone makes a huge difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T01:50:41-08:00","id":381681,"title":"","content":"From what I see in the RAW you can only use Embeds and Exploits on the interior of the house unless you get an exceptional success on the activation roll, at which point you can move objects as if with telekinesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:12:19-08:00","id":382546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/381134-boo-ma-no-hands-demon-house-and-manipulating-stuff?p=381558#post381558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it allow form abilities? That alone makes a huge difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon House makes no mention of form abilities. However, it mentions that Angels and Demons can take inanimate objects up to and including buildings <i>as Covers</i>, so I see no reason why an Unchained shouldn't be allowed to manifest a form ability during the duration of Demon House, though I would rule once manifested, a form ability is &quot;fixed&quot; in position until the Exploit ends, so if a Unchained makes the coal chute his Cavernous Maw (cool way to get rid of a body) it stays there until he uses Demon House again.<br /> <br /> Some form abilities are obviously made redundant by the effects of the Demon House ( you don't need Night Vision when you can see everything in the building at all times)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}